    "likely_right_file": "bhel/Part1.pdf",
    "likely_right_page": 44,
    "why": "Both Part1.pdf (p. 44) and Part4.pdf (p. 61) explicitly state the operating arrangement as 1W+1S (one working, one standby). Part3.pdf (p. 146) states 2X100%, which describes the same total capacity (two 100% capacity pumps) using different notation rather than conflicting on the physical design, though 1W+1S is clearer for the proposed change to 1 working + 2 standby.",
    "consequence": "If 2X100% is misunderstood to mean two pumps running simultaneously rather than one working and one standby, adding a third pump could result in undersized pumps or overloaded discharge piping and electrical systems if multiple 100% pumps are run at the same time."
